<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-4">4 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Zhao Kuangyin founds the Song dynasty</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Proclaimed emperor by his troops at Chenqiao, the general became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song">Emperor Taizu of Song</a>. The dynasty reunited most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and presided over remarkable advances in commerce, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> and technology.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song">Emperor Taizu of Song</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolution</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/chenqiao-mutiny">Chenqiao Mutiny</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Chenqiao Mutiny was the coup of 960 CE in which troops of the Later Zhou commander Zhao Kuangyin draped him in the imperial yellow robe and proclaimed him emperor.</p></div></li></ol></section>
